#!/usr/bin/env python3
# =============================================================================
# h96-emulators - opt-in game-emulator suite installer for the H96 Max V58
#                 (RK3588 / Mali-G610, all-open Panthor/PanVK stack).
#
# Installs nothing by default. Emulators are pulled on demand so non-gamers carry
# no weight and no game code is ever bundled. Bring your own game dumps/BIOS.
#
#   h96-emulators                       interactive multi-select menu
#   h96-emulators list                  catalog + install state + GPU backend
#   h96-emulators install <names...|all>
#   h96-emulators remove  <names...|all>
#   h96-emulators bootstrap             install flatpak + Flathub (fresh flashes)
#   h96-emulators gpu                   report GPU wiring (PanVK/Panfrost vs software)
#
# The suite (GPU-accelerated systems only - each offloads real 3D rendering to the
# Mali-G610 through PanVK / Panfrost; verified on the box, see `h96-emulators gpu`):
#   retroarch  Multi-system, Vulkan/glcore cores (PS1/N64/PSP/Saturn) - Flatpak
#   dolphin    GameCube / Wii            (Vulkan PanVK)                - Flatpak
#   ppsspp     Sony PSP                  (Vulkan PanVK)                - Flatpak
#   flycast    Sega Dreamcast / NAOMI    (Vulkan / GL)                 - Flatpak
#   melonds    Nintendo DS               (OpenGL 3D renderer)         - Flatpak
#   rmg        Nintendo 64 (Parallel-RDP Vulkan)                       - Flatpak
#   azahar     Nintendo 3DS              (Vulkan PanVK)                - Flatpak
#   cemu       Nintendo Wii U            (Vulkan PanVK, box64, no wine)- box64
#
# CPU-RENDERED SYSTEMS ARE NOT INCLUDED HERE, ON PURPOSE. mGBA (Game Boy Advance) and
# ScummVM (point-and-click adventures) are 2D: they do not meaningfully use the Mali GPU,
# so there is nothing for this tool's GPU wiring to do for them. They are NOT missing from
# the box - both are already one click away in the software store (Discover), as aarch64
# Flatpaks on Flathub (io.mgba.mGBA, org.scummvm.ScummVM) and as apt packages (mgba-qt,
# scummvm). Install them there; they run fine on the CPU.
#
# The seven Flatpaks are native ARM64 and render on the GPU through PanVK/Panfrost.
# Cemu has no ARM build, so it runs the x86-64 build under box64 (Vulkan -> PanVK).
# `install` runs a GPU wiring + verification pass so each emulator actually uses the
# Mali GPU (not the llvmpipe software fallback); see gpu_wire()/gpu_probe().
#
# GPU: pick the recommended backend (shown by `list`) inside each emulator. On this
# open Panfrost/PanVK stack, Vulkan (PanVK) is preferred where supported; a few use
# OpenGL ES (Panfrost). Flatpak GPU acceleration relies on the runtime's Mesa having
# Panfrost/PanVK - verify per emulator that it is NOT falling back to software.
#
# FRESH FLASHES have no flatpak. Running an install auto-bootstraps it (apt install
# flatpak + Flathub remote) after a warning; or run `h96-emulators bootstrap` first.
# Auto-elevates via sudo. Cemu files land under the invoking desktop user's home.
# =============================================================================
import os, sys, shutil, subprocess, tempfile, json, urllib.request, pwd

